1. User accounts and onboarding
1. Sign up / Log in — Email, Google, or Apple authentication.
2. User profile — Name, avatar, learning statistics, and preferences.
3. Learning goals — Travel, business, HSK preparation, studying abroad, or casual learning.
4. Chinese proficiency selection — Complete beginner, intermediate, or advanced.
5. Placement test — Determine the user's initial Chinese proficiency.
6. Daily learning goal — Choose a target of 5, 10, 15, 20, or 30 minutes.
7. Personalized learning path — Lessons adapted to goals and current proficiency.
8. Simplified / Traditional Chinese selection — Choose the preferred writing system.
9. Native language selection — Change the language used for explanations and translations.
10. Onboarding tutorial — Introduce the learning interface and core functionality.
2. Learning curriculum and lessons
11. Structured learning roadmap — Progress through beginner, intermediate, and advanced material.
12. HSK-aligned curriculum — Organize lessons around the HSK proficiency framework.
13. Thematic lessons — Greetings, numbers, food, travel, shopping, work, and more.
14. Short interactive lessons — Bite-sized sessions of approximately 3–10 minutes.
15. Vocabulary introduction — Learn new words with translations and examples.
16. Grammar lessons — Explain Chinese sentence structures and grammatical rules.
17. Sentence-building exercises — Arrange words into correct sentences.
18. Translation exercises — Translate Chinese to English and vice versa.
19. Multiple-choice questions — Select the correct Chinese word, sound, or meaning.
20. Fill-in-the-blank exercises — Complete sentences with missing words.
3. Vocabulary and reading
21. Vocabulary dictionary — Search Chinese words and their definitions.
22. Pinyin display — Show pronunciation using Romanized Chinese.
23. Tone-mark display — Show tones using standard pinyin diacritics.
24. Word audio playback — Hear individual words pronounced.
25. Example sentences — Learn vocabulary through realistic contexts.
26. Word frequency indicators — Identify commonly used Chinese words.
27. Vocabulary categories — Organize words by topic and difficulty.
28. Saved vocabulary — Bookmark words for later review.
29. Interactive reading passages — Read short stories and dialogues.
30. Tap-to-translate reading — Tap unfamiliar characters or words to view their meanings.
4. Listening and pronunciation
31. Native-speaker audio — Listen to natural Mandarin pronunciation.
32. Four-tone training — Practice the four Mandarin tones.
33. Neutral-tone training — Recognize and produce the neutral tone.
34. Tone recognition quizzes — Identify tones from audio.
35. Tone-pair exercises — Practice common combinations of two tones.
36. Tone-sandhi lessons — Learn pronunciation changes, including third-tone sandhi.
37. Speech recording — Record pronunciation through the microphone.
38. Pronunciation feedback — Receive feedback on spoken Chinese.
39. Slow audio playback — Reduce playback speed for difficult phrases.
40. Listening comprehension exercises — Answer questions after hearing sentences or conversations.
5. Chinese characters and handwriting
41. Hanzi character lessons — Learn characters and their meanings.
42. Animated stroke order — Show the correct sequence of strokes.
43. Handwriting practice — Draw characters using a finger, mouse, or stylus.
44. Stroke-order correction — Detect incorrect stroke sequences.
45. Character recognition quizzes — Match characters with their meanings.
46. Radical lessons — Understand the components of Chinese characters.
47. Character decomposition — Break complex characters into meaningful components.
48. Character similarity exercises — Distinguish visually similar characters.
49. Character etymology — Explain the historical origins of selected characters.
50. Character-writing challenges — Practice writing characters from memory.
6. Grammar and sentence construction
51. Grammar reference library — Search explanations of grammatical structures.
52. Sentence pattern lessons — Learn common patterns such as subject–verb–object.
53. Measure-word lessons — Practice classifiers such as 个, 本, and 张.
54. Word-order exercises — Practice natural Chinese sentence structure.
55. Question formation — Learn how to ask questions in Mandarin.
56. Negation exercises — Practice 不, 没, and related structures.
57. Aspect particle lessons — Understand 了, 过, and 着.
58. Grammar mistake explanations — Explain why an answer is incorrect.
59. Sentence transformations — Convert affirmative, negative, and interrogative sentences.
60. Context-based grammar quizzes — Select appropriate grammar in real situations.
7. Flashcards, revision, and assessments
61. Spaced repetition system (SRS) — Schedule reviews based on recall performance.
62. Flashcard decks — Study words, characters, and sentences.
63. Custom flashcards — Create personalized vocabulary cards.
64. Audio flashcards — Listen before revealing written answers.
65. Reverse flashcards — Practice both recognition and active recall.
66. Daily review queue — Show vocabulary and concepts due for review.
67. Weak-word detection — Identify words the learner repeatedly forgets.
68. Mistake notebook — Save incorrect answers for targeted practice.
69. Lesson completion quizzes — Test learning after each lesson.
70. Progressive assessments — Evaluate skills at the end of each unit or level.
8. AI-powered learning features
71. AI Mandarin tutor — Chat with an AI tutor to ask questions about Chinese.
72. AI conversation practice — Practice realistic written conversations.
73. AI voice conversation — Practice spoken Mandarin through voice interaction.
74. AI role-playing scenarios — Simulate ordering food, visiting a doctor, or interviewing for a job.
75. AI grammar correction — Correct user-written sentences and explain mistakes.
76. AI sentence explanations — Break down unfamiliar sentences into components.
77. AI vocabulary examples — Generate personalized example sentences.
78. AI-adaptive lesson difficulty — Adjust learning difficulty according to performance.
79. AI-generated quizzes — Create exercises based on recently learned vocabulary.
80. AI study recommendations — Suggest what to review or study next.
9. Gamification and motivation
81. Experience points (XP) — Earn points by completing learning activities.
82. Daily streaks — Track consecutive days of learning.
83. Achievements and badges — Reward important learning milestones.
84. Learning levels — Unlock higher levels through progress.
85. Daily challenges — Complete special exercises for rewards.
86. Weekly challenges — Work toward longer-term learning goals.
87. Leaderboards — Compare learning activity with other users.
88. Study reminders — Receive notifications to practice.
89. Progress celebrations — Display animations after milestones or completed lessons.
90. Personal learning milestones — Celebrate learning 100 words, finishing a course, or passing an assessment.
10. Progress tracking and analytics
91. Learning dashboard — Overview of progress, goals, and upcoming lessons.
92. Vocabulary mastered counter — Track words and characters learned.
93. Study time tracking — Record daily, weekly, and monthly learning time.
94. Skills breakdown — Show progress in listening, speaking, reading, and writing.
95. Accuracy statistics — Display performance across exercises.
96. Learning activity calendar — Visualize study consistency.
97. Personalized progress reports — Summarize achievements and difficulties.
98. HSK readiness estimates — Estimate readiness based on relevant skill assessments.
99. Learning history — Review completed lessons, quizzes, and past results.
100. Goal completion tracking — Track progress toward personal learning targets.
11. User experience and accessibility
101. Responsive design — Support desktop, tablet, and mobile screens.
102. Progressive Web App (PWA) — Allow installation from a browser.
103. Dark mode — Provide light and dark display themes.
104. Offline learning — Download supported lessons and study without internet.
105. Cross-device synchronization — Continue learning across multiple devices.
106. Adjustable text size — Make Hanzi and other text easier to read.
107. Pinyin visibility toggle — Show or hide pinyin while studying.
108. Audio playback controls — Repeat recordings, change playback speed, and control volume.
109. Accessibility support — Support keyboard navigation, screen readers, and sufficient contrast.
110. Search and navigation — Quickly find lessons, vocabulary, and learning materials.
12. Administration, content management, and monetization
111. Admin dashboard — Manage learners, learning content, and application settings.
112. Course management system — Create and organize lessons and units.
113. Vocabulary management — Add, edit, import, and categorize vocabulary.
114. Audio content management — Upload and manage pronunciation recordings.
115. Quiz management — Create exercises and configure correct answers.
116. Content quality review — Check translations, pinyin, grammar, and audio before publishing.
117. User feedback system — Let learners report errors and suggest improvements.
118. Subscription management — Support free and premium plans.
119. Payment integration — Process subscriptions and manage billing.
120. Analytics, security, and backups — Monitor application performance, protect user information, and maintain reliable backups.
